== norm classes (trivial <=> function-level identity possible) ==
  d_A is a square in Q(R,m): false
  d_B is a square in Q(R,m): false
  d_A*d_B is a square in Q(R,m): false
conclusion: if all false, NO base twist makes any V or V*V a
function-field square: the second-stage wall is arithmetic
(point-dependent), not a constant-class identity.

